As of October 2026, the latest Java version is Java 27 (JDK 27). It was released on September 15, 2026.

Current Java releases
Version	Released	LTS?	Importance
Java 8	2014	✅	Legacy/very common
Java 11	2018	✅	Enterprise
Java 17	2021	✅	Very common
Java 21	2023	✅	⭐ Modern enterprise
Java 25	2025	✅	⭐ Latest LTS
Java 26	Mar 2026	❌	Feature release
Java 27	Sep 2026	❌	Latest

Oracle currently identifies JDK 27 as the latest Java SE release, while JDK 25 is the latest LTS release.

For your interviews

I would focus in this order:

Java 8 → 11 → 17 → 21 → 25

You should know Java 27 exists, but for a Java/Spring Boot interview, Java 17, 21 and 25 are much more important than memorizing every Java 27 feature.

Oracle Java Downloads

java 27 feature

Yes. Java 27 / JDK 27 was released on September 15, 2026. It is a feature release, not LTS; Java 25 remains the latest LTS.

For your Java/Spring Boot interview preparation, these are the important Java 27 features:

1. Primitive Types in Patterns — Preview ⭐⭐⭐⭐

Java 27 continues the evolution of pattern matching to allow primitive types in instanceof, switch, and other pattern contexts.

For example, the direction is toward:

switch (value) {
    case int i -> System.out.println("int: " + i);
    case long l -> System.out.println("long: " + l);
    default -> System.out.println("other");
}

This is the 5th preview in Java 27, so don't call it a finalized Java 27 feature in an interview.

2. Lazy Constants — Preview ⭐⭐⭐

Lazy constants provide immutable values whose initialization can happen later.

Conceptually:

final field
   ↓
initialized during construction

Lazy Constant
   ↓
initialized when needed
   ↓
remains immutable

The JVM can treat them as true constants for optimization. Java 27 has the third preview of this API.

3. Structured Concurrency — Preview ⭐⭐⭐⭐

This is particularly interesting for your microservices interviews.

Suppose one request calls three services:

Order Request
    |
    +-- Customer Service
    |
    +-- Payment Service
    |
    +-- Inventory Service

Structured concurrency allows these related tasks to be treated as one unit of work, making cancellation, error handling and observability easier.

Java 27 has the 7th preview of Structured Concurrency.

4. Vector API — Incubator ⭐⭐

The Vector API allows Java applications to express vector computations that can compile to optimized CPU vector instructions.

Useful for:

High-performance computing
Machine learning
Scientific calculations
Image/data processing

Java 27 has the 12th incubator of this API.

5. Post-Quantum Hybrid Key Exchange ⭐⭐⭐

Java 27 improves TLS 1.3 security with hybrid key exchange algorithms combining traditional cryptography with quantum-resistant algorithms.

The important point for an interview:

Java 27 adds post-quantum protection to TLS 1.3 communication.

Applications using the standard javax.net.ssl APIs can benefit without changing existing application code.

6. Compact Object Headers — Default ⭐⭐⭐

This is a JVM performance improvement.

Java 27 makes Compact Object Headers enabled by default.

Object headers on supported 64-bit architectures are reduced from 96 bits to 64 bits, which can reduce heap usage and improve data locality.

Think:

Before:
Object Header → 96 bits

Java 27:
Object Header → 64 bits
7. G1 is Default Garbage Collector in All Environments ⭐⭐⭐

Java 27 makes G1 (Garbage-First) GC the default collector in all environments, rather than only server environments.

For an interview:

G1 is the default garbage collector across environments in JDK 27.

8. JFR In-Process Data Redaction ⭐⭐

Java Flight Recorder gets improved security.

It can redact sensitive information such as:

command-line arguments
initial environment variables
initial system properties

before that data leaves the process.

9. PEM Encodings — Preview ⭐⭐

Java 27 continues the PEM API as a third preview.

It supports encoding/decoding cryptographic objects such as:

Private keys
Public keys
Certificates
Certificate Revocation Lists

into/from PEM format.

🔥 Java 21 → 25 → 27

For your interview preparation, remember it like this:

Java 21
   ↓
Virtual Threads
Record Patterns
Pattern Matching switch
Sequenced Collections

Java 25 LTS
   ↓
Module Import
Compact Source Files
Flexible Constructor Bodies
Scoped Values
Structured Concurrency

Java 27
   ↓
Primitive Patterns
Lazy Constants
Structured Concurrency improvements
Vector API
Post-Quantum TLS
Compact Object Headers
G1 default everywhere
JFR security improvements
⭐ What you should actually prepare

For a Java + Spring Boot + MicroservicesDesignPattern Lead/Senior interview, I'd prioritize:

Java 21
→ Virtual Threads ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Java 25
→ Scoped Values ⭐⭐⭐⭐
→ Structured Concurrency ⭐⭐⭐⭐

Java 27
→ Primitive Types in Patterns ⭐⭐⭐
→ Compact Object Headers ⭐⭐⭐
→ G1 changes ⭐⭐⭐
→ Post-Quantum TLS ⭐⭐

Don't spend too much time memorizing Java 27 preview/incubator features—the LTS versions 17, 21 and 25 are more important for enterprise interviews.